WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/components/ai/AIBatteryHealthForecastNarrative.tsx — the Helix battery-health forecast
  narrator card. It is `withAiFeature('battery-health-forecast-narrative', InnerSection)` (a
  `useAiEnabled` gate; disabled ⇒ the HOC renders `null`). InnerSection uses `useTranslation` +
  `useAiStream({ url: '/ai/battery/health/narrate', body: { vehicle_id: Number.isFinite(numericVehicleId)
  ? numericVehicleId : 0 }, onEvent: noop })` and renders the shared `AIFeatureCard` with title
  `t('battery.aiNarrative.title','Explain the battery health forecast')`, a description, button
  `t('battery.aiNarrative.generateButton','Narrate forecast')`, badge
  `t('battery.aiNarrative.badge','Helix')`, `canStart = Number.isFinite(numericVehicleId) &&
  numericVehicleId > 0`, and the stream handle.

  TWO parity differences from the 0005 predecessor (AIAnomalyExplanations), reproduced faithfully and
  disclosed here (rule 9, no silent drift):
    • body has NO `days` field — narrate posts only `{ vehicle_id }` (0005's explain posts
      `{ vehicle_id, days: 30 }`).
    • canStart requires `numericVehicleId > 0` (mirrors the handler-side `vehicle_id > 0` parser), a
      stricter gate than 0005's `vehicleId != null`. id 0 / nil / negative keep the button disabled.

  Composed shared primitives reproduced for parity (their native atoms are owned by the P4 component-
  library bundle — out of scope here and not yet present — so they are reproduced as private subviews
  scoped to this surface, the only files this prompt may touch):
    • AIFeatureCard  : GlassPanel → (title + AIBadge) → description → universal "Ask Helix" button
                       (idle "Ask Helix" / streaming "Helix is thinking…"; disabled = !canStart ||
                       isStreaming; aria-label "Ask Helix · {buttonLabel}") → AiOutputPanel.
    • AiOutputPanel  : nothing while idle+empty; "Helix error: {message}" in error; AIThinkingIndicator
                       (shimmer lines + dots) while streaming before the first delta; else the prose.
    • useAiStream    : idle → streaming → (done | error); `delta.text` frames accumulate; a non-OK HTTP
                       response finalises as "stream_http_{status}"; unknown SSE event types dropped.

